# {{ project_name }}

From here the team builds features across the {{ project_name }} repositories with one agent, one OpenSpec and one set of checks. The code stays in the application repositories, cloned into `repos/`; this repository holds the agent rules, specs, decisions and checks. It is generated from the [sdd-metarepo](https://github.com/cmdtorch/sdd-metarepo) Copier template, with [sdd-kit](https://github.com/cmdtorch/sdd_kit) on top of OpenSpec.

## Quick start

You need [mise](https://mise.jdx.dev) and git (mise installs Node and the other tools), and access to the repositories listed in `repos.toml` (usually an SSH key added to GitHub).

```sh
git clone git@github.com:{{ github_org }}/{{ project_slug }}.git
cd {{ project_slug }}
mise trust
mise run setup
```

`setup` installs the root tools and the meta-repository's git hooks, installs sdd-kit when the project has none yet, writes `mise.lock` when it is missing, asks for the repositories when `repos.toml` is empty, clones each repository into `repos/<name>` on its rest branch, and installs their dependencies and git hooks with their own commands. A repeated run is safe: existing clones are left as they are.

After `setup`, create each application's environment files as described in [docs/agents/environment.md](docs/agents/environment.md), then check everything with `mise run check`.

## Right after generation

1. Add the repositories with `mise run add-repo`; the first `setup` asks for them. Each gets an entry in `repos.toml`, task stubs `mise run <name>:test|check|run|install` and rows in the generated tables.
2. Start Claude Code in the root and run `/bootstrap`, the AI onboarding. It reads each clone, configures its mise tasks with the clone's own commands, fills in the docs (command tables, environment notes, glossary) and the OpenSpec context, and asks questions with options where the clone leaves something open. `/bootstrap <name>` onboards a repository added later.
3. Commit everything, including the sdd-kit files, on a branch and open a pull request.

