## Tasks

| Command | What it does |
| --- | --- |
| `mise run setup` | Hooks, sdd-kit, `mise.lock`, repositories, clones, clone dependencies and hooks |
| `mise run add-repo` | Adds repositories to `repos.toml`, regenerates the lists, offers to clone |
| `mise run repos:sync` | Regenerates everything that lists the repositories from `repos.toml` |
| `mise run clone` | Clones the missing clones |
| `mise run pull` | `git pull --rebase --autostash` in the meta-repository and each clone on its branch |
| `mise run status` | Branch and number of changed files in each clone |
| `mise run check` | Each clone's own checks, `ast-grep` rules, registry comparison |
| `mise run lint` | `rumdl`, `typos`, `agnix` and the agent files in the root |
| `mise run test` | Meta-repository tests |
| `mise run kit:install`, `mise run kit:update` | Install or update sdd-kit and pin its OpenSpec version |
| `mise run <name>:*` | A clone's commands, listed in `AGENTS.md` |

## Keeping up to date

| What | How |
| --- | --- |
| This template's improvements | `mise x uv@latest -- uvx copier update --trust`, then review the diff; the answers live in `.copier-answers.yml` |
| sdd-kit | `mise run kit:update`, then commit `openspec/`, `.claude/`, `.gitignore` and `mise.toml` |
| Repositories | `mise run add-repo`, or edit `repos.toml` and run `mise run repos:sync` |

## Working with the agent

Start the agent from the meta-repository root. Begin a new feature with `/opsx:new`; sdd-kit takes it through questions, specs, design, tasks and checks. {% if agent_git_default == 'on' %}The agent commits and pushes on work branches unless you turn it off for yourself{% else %}The agent does not commit or push until you enable it for yourself{% endif %} ([docs/agents/agent-settings.md](docs/agents/agent-settings.md)).
